 "chain_follow": {
  "hair": "hair chains hang from Head; the lowest hair keeps 50% on UpperChest, so a turned head twists the hair at the neck rather than swinging it off the back; hair lying on a cape takes the cape's weights and moves with it.",
  "skirt": "skirt panels hang from the thighs, so a step lifts the cloth by itself (no runtime needed); where the cloth reaches below the knees, each panel goes on down the shin as a second chain (<panel>Low0..), so the cloth drapes down bent knees; it turns from the thigh chain to the shin chain level with the knee behind and beside it and a little below the knee in front, so it tents over a bent knee. Cloth in front of the thighs rides on them fully; the back and the sides keep a share on Hips above the knee (all of it at the hinge, 30% further down, none by the knee of a long skirt and none where the cloth touches a thigh). Across the front and the back the cloth goes with the leg it hangs over, blending from one leg to the other only in the gap between them. The springs in the game add sway on the chains."
 },
