 "socket_frames": "a prop's origin in the fist (grip), its +Y along the business end and +X along the edge, as the kit's weapon Frame (o, ax, sd): parent it to the socket with no offset",
 "owner_rules": {
  "out": "held things and world props: left out of the rig (held props become their own files, on the hand sockets)",
  "head": "worn on or part of the head (beards, ears, horns, hats, helmets, face parts): Head",
  "head_drape": "hair, hoods, headscarves and veils: Head above the middle of the neck, UpperChest below it (long hair lies on the back)",
  "drape": "capes, cloaks, mantles, shawls, fur collars and stoles: UpperChest (they hang from the shoulders)",
  "back": "gear on the back (sheathed two-handers, quivers, shields, packs, bedrolls, baldrics): UpperChest",
  "hip": "gear hanging at the belt (sheathed blades, pouches, keys, books, satchels): Hips, never a leg or an arm; straps higher up follow the trunk",
  "trunk": "sleeveless garments, belts and jewellery on the body: the trunk bones only, never a limb or the head",
  "neck": "collars and neck cloths: the trunk or the Neck, never a limb",
  "skirt": "skirts, aprons, tabards and tassets: the trunk and the thighs; below the knee they stay on the thigh, unless they hug the shin or foot (within 2 voxels)",
  "robe": "robes and long coats: any bone but the head; below the knee their hem stays on the thigh, but what hugs the shin or foot (a robe's own boots) stays there",
  "leg": "trousers, boots and leggings: the trunk and the legs, never an arm",
  "sleeve": "sleeves, gloves, bracers, pauldrons and bangles: the arms only",
  "skin": "the bare body: its nearest body segment",
  "body": "everything else: its nearest body segment, but never the head or the neck (a collar stays on the body)",
  "limb_core": "over all of these (but held things and the head): whatever lies inside an arm's or a leg's own volume (half a voxel in, past the shoulder and hip balls) follows that limb, so a moving limb stays whole",
  "outfits": "a part that paints a whole outfit (robes, vestments, the clothes sets) is sorted by material first: its boots follow the leg rule, its rope or cord belt the trunk rule, the hands it repaints the skin rule",
  "joint_cuts": "elbows, wrists and knees are cut by a plane halving the angle between the limb's two segments, ankles by a plane across the shin; past the wrist only the hand itself (and a glove) goes with the hand, a sleeve's mouth stays on the forearm",
  "shin_plates": "knee cops ride whole on the shin",
  "belts_through_limbs": "belts, sashes and jewellery (the trunk rule) that pass through a limb hanging against the body stay with the trunk (the limb-core rule gives way: the limb gets a small dent instead)",
  "cloth_by_the_hands": "robe or garment cloth by a hanging forearm or hand that the figure built with its arms out also has is cloth, not sleeve: it goes to the trunk, or below the hips to the skirt",
  "skirt_chains": "cloth below the hips (skirts, robes, coats, aprons, and belts, stoles and sashes hanging over them) goes on the skirt panels (on the thighs, and below the knee on down the shins); an outfit's own trousers stay on the legs",
  "cape_chains": "capes and cloaks go on the cape chains (blending into the chest at the shoulders, and where they lie over an arm riding on that arm)",
  "hair_chains": "hair, hoods and veils hanging more than 0.45 head radii below the head's centre go on the hair chains when they hang 10 voxels or more (hair lying on a cape moves with the cape); shorter hangs follow the neck band"
 },
